  "subject": "a matchmaking auntie in a city park carries forty paper resumes, notices two of her clients, a bus mechanic and a pharmacist, both walk the same path at six every morning, and quietly moves her folding stool until they have to sit beside each other",
  "caption": "Mandarin Irish folk session, gentle lilting 6/8 jig feel. Fiddle plays a warm singing melody with light ornaments, tin whistle doubles the hook an octave up, steel-string acoustic guitar strums open DADGAD-style chords, bodhran taps soft downbeats with a brush stick. Intimate pub-corner room, natural reverb, unpolished. Female voice, clear mid-high register, warm folk delivery, melody clearly sung. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 92 BPM, G major. Gentle, humorous, hopeful mood. No electronic beats, no autotune, no rap, no synth pads, no bagpipes.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - tin whistle melody, fiddle enters]\n\n[Verse 1]\n我提著一袋四十張履歷\n每張都寫著年紀和興趣\n修公車的他寫著愛散步\n賣藥的她也寫愛散步\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n天亮六點整\n同一條小路\n\n[Chorus]\n我把小板凳搬一搬\n搬到長椅的中間\n我只是個阿姨\n坐在這裡剛剛好\n\n[Verse 2]\n他每天走到橋邊就回頭\n她每天走到橋邊也回頭\n一個往東一個往西\n中間隔著一排矮樹\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我咳了一聲\n他們抬起頭\n\n[Chorus]\n我把小板凳搬一搬\n搬到長椅的盡頭\n他說借過她說請坐\n我站起來剛剛好\n\n[Outro - fiddle sustains, tin whistle fades out]",
